\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Tag Copy and Tag Copy/Delete Original are mutually exclusive inventory copy modes. Checking either box only selects the mode. After you click Inventory, TLO opens the same destination-entry window and requires an existing full path with readable available-space information. Tag Copy states that originals are retained. Tag Copy/Delete Original adds the warning that originals are removed after verified transfer. Before any transfer, TLO builds the show group and extracts metadata from the original source tree, including original folder and path text, selected setlist content, music filenames, and existing audio tags. It then copies or moves the identified show folder and uses the destination path for tagging and final inventory output. The transfer always applies to the complete identified folder tree: every file and every folder beneath it is included, including non-music files and empty subfolders. Tag Copy always totals the source and checks destination capacity because it always creates another tree. Copy/Delete Original performs that source-size capacity check only when the destination is on a different partition; a same-partition Copy/Delete Original operation is a directory rename or move and does not total or compare file sizes. Real copies are verified by relative file paths and sizes and by descendant folder structure before processing continues or a Copy/Delete source is removed. When a compliant Show/folder name collides with an existing same-base folder, TLO does not call the new folder a copy merely because the name is already present. It first compares the complete recursive trees. A (copyN) suffix is used only when the same relative folders, the same relative files, the same file sizes, and the byte contents of every file are identical. Same-size files with different bytes, an extra or missing file, or an extra or missing folder make the new item an (altN) instead. File timestamps do not affect this decision. An existing folder already named with (copyN) is also rechecked during inventory; if it does not exactly match another same-base sibling tree, the Show is identified with (altN) instead. For Tag Copy/Delete Original, the selected destination parent is only the container that receives transferred shows; it is not permission to re-inventory every previously inventoried show below that parent. Existing destination bootlist/setlist entries remain in place, and only an existing row whose complete destination volume and path exactly match a show path produced by the current Copy/Delete run may be replaced.}
