Acceptable corruption % controls when corruption removes the entire logical show. The value is 0-100 and defaults to 100; the whole-show threshold is exceeded only when corrupt * 100 is greater than acceptable_percent * total, so equality is allowed. Regardless of that setting, a logical show with no readable audio is sent to Trash/Recycle Bin, and any individual music folder whose directly contained audio files are all corrupt is also sent to Trash/Recycle Bin when the rest of the logical show remains. Every other detected corrupt audio file is sent to Trash/Recycle Bin individually before later tagging/copy/rename processing. TLO never permanently deletes as a Trash fallback. Dry run reports the planned whole-folder, all-corrupt-folder, and individual-file actions without changing anything.}
